--- !u!114 &125263210
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 125263208}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 533b0f69328994212a8c560d8f3528c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: MyGame.Runtime::MyGame.Lingerer
  id: hesper
  displayName: Old Hesper
  keepsake: hesper-boat-lantern
  fare: 100
  interactRadius: 1
  waitAt: {fileID: 746980633}
  heldKeepsake: {fileID: 113362790}
  kept: {fileID: 526145462}
  meeting:
  - Oh. You're not him.
  - Forgive me. I keep a lamp here for my boy. He went out the night the water came up, and he hasn't found his way back.
  - I saw his light, though. Out on the water, on the little deck north of the yard. Burning, all this time.
  - I can't reach it. My old legs were never for water. But you... you carry the Ferryman's things, don't you?
  - If you could bring it to me. I'd know him by it.
  waiting:
  - His light's still out there. On the little deck, north of the yard.
  waitingWithoutHook:
  - There's no bridge. There never was. The Ferryman used to cross with a hook, you know.
  given:
  - That's it. That's his.
  - He painted the glass himself. Crooked, see? He never could hold a brush still.
  - It's still warm.
  - Then he didn't go astray. He went across. He must have. The light's still burning.
  - I can let him go now. I can go too.
  fareAsked:
  - They say the crossing costs a coin. I have none. I spent them all on oil.
  fareAgain:
  - The crossing costs a coin, they say. I've nothing left but oil.
  paid:
  - Thank you, child.
  - I remember the Ferryman slowing, every night, to wave at my lamp. Then one night he didn't. Not a wave. Not a look.
  - I'll wait by the boat. When you're ready to row, I'll be there.
  ready:
  - The boat's there, and I'm ready. Whenever you are.
  payLabel: Pay her fare
  declineLabel: Not yet
